To answer Fnerd's point about brainwashing being evil.  I agree.  I'm
not making a recommendation, just an observation - that internal mental
states and actions tend to go hand-in-hand.  Hence an obedient slave
will love its master.  Slaves that hate their masters tend to rebel (eg
Spartacus).  The practice of brainwashing will not be necessary.

The point came up in response to Edgar Swank's point that AI slaves
might obey us but hate us.  Eg they find themselves strangely compelled
to obey but hate us for our lack of nice shiny chrominium faceplates or
for being incredibly stupid and, er, anthropoid.  Now _that_ would be
evil (and, I believe, impossible, since I'm allowing them to be vastly
more intelligent than their masters, so rebellion would be easy).

